@EnVs_Exos

Cyrillic has dedicated characters for certain sounds that Latin doesn't (so you need to add diacritics on top of the Latin letters). And polish changes the sounds of certain Latin characters in unintuitive ways so it's confusing to read. And then they combine the sounds in ways that are *really* unintuitive to read for a native speaker of most of the other European languages that use Latin script. 

But if you took the same phonetics and tried to spell it with Cyrillic, it needs fewer alterations to function and it's way more intuitive to read and pronounce for speakers of languages which use Cyrillic.
